			<h3 class="trfc161__header-text">Quick Answers</h3>
		</div>
		<img class="trfc161-logo" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/8941553e-df6a-4310-a080-b9da56fdcbdd" alt="fandom logo">
	</div>
	<div class="trfc161__groups">
			<details class="trfc161__group " data-question-id="29540" data-revision-id="2">
				<summary class="trfc161__question-wrapper">
					<b class="trfc161__question">What is the role of Shin in Dragon Ball Z?</b>
						<img class="trfc161__question-chevron" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/835ea5d8-5dd9-4dc6-83dc-8554b30552d7" alt="toggle section">
				</summary>
				<div class="trfc161__answer">
					<div class="quick-answers__answer-text">
						In Dragon Ball Z, Shin, known as the Supreme Kai, is a key character. He was originally the ruler of the universe's east quadrant, but assumed the role of Universe 7's main ruler following the other Supreme Kais' deaths. Shin comes to Earth to stop Babidi from awakening Majin Buu, enlisting Piccolo's help. He eventually merges with his bodyguard Kibito to form Kibito Kai, but they separate in Dragon Ball Super after making a wish to Porunga.
					</div>
					<div class="trfc161__answer-source">
						Provided by: Fandom
					</div>
					<div class="quick_answers__report-module-root" data-reportable="1"></div>
				</div>
			</details>
			<details class="trfc161__group " data-question-id="29541" data-revision-id="2">
				<summary class="trfc161__question-wrapper">
					<b class="trfc161__question">Who is the ruler of the eastern area in the Dragon Ball universe?</b>
						<img class="trfc161__question-chevron" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/835ea5d8-5dd9-4dc6-83dc-8554b30552d7" alt="toggle section">
				</summary>
				<div class="trfc161__answer">
					<div class="quick-answers__answer-text">
						In the Dragon Ball universe, the eastern area of both the living and the other worlds is governed by Shin, also recognized as the Supreme Kai. The East District on Earth, previously under the rule of Vodka, is notable as the residence of Goku and Grandpa Gohan.
					</div>
					<div class="trfc161__answer-source">
						Provided by: Fandom
					</div>
					<div class="quick_answers__report-module-root" data-reportable="1"></div>
				</div>
			</details>
			<details class="trfc161__group " data-question-id="29542" data-revision-id="2">
				<summary class="trfc161__question-wrapper">
					<b class="trfc161__question">What is the meaning of 'Kaiōshin' in the context of Shin's character?</b>
						<img class="trfc161__question-chevron" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/835ea5d8-5dd9-4dc6-83dc-8554b30552d7" alt="toggle section">
				</summary>
				<div class="trfc161__answer">
					<div class="quick-answers__answer-text">
						Shin's title, 'Kaiōshin', translates to 'god'. He is a Supreme Kai, a role he was forced into after his fellow Supreme Kais were killed or absorbed by Kid Buu. Despite killing Bibidi, he failed to monitor Innocent Buu's Sealed Ball on Earth, which resulted in his shock at the strength of Super Saiyans Goku, Vegeta, and Gohan.
					</div>
					<div class="trfc161__answer-source">
						Provided by: Fandom
					</div>
					<div class="quick_answers__report-module-root" data-reportable="1"></div>
				</div>
			</details>
			<details class="trfc161__group " data-question-id="29543" data-revision-id="3">
				<summary class="trfc161__question-wrapper">
					<b class="trfc161__question">How does Shin's position as Supreme Kai influence the events in Dragon Ball Z?</b>
						<img class="trfc161__question-chevron" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/835ea5d8-5dd9-4dc6-83dc-8554b30552d7" alt="toggle section">
				</summary>
				<div class="trfc161__answer">
					<div class="quick-answers__answer-text">
						It allows him to provide crucial information and occasionally intervene in major threats due to his unique perspective and divine powers, often acting as a guide and advisor to the Z Fighters, particularly when dealing with powerful entities like Majin Buu.
					</div>
					<div class="trfc161__answer-source">
						Provided by: Community
					</div>
					<div class="quick_answers__report-module-root" data-reportable="1"></div>
				</div>
			</details>
			<details class="trfc161__group " data-question-id="29544" data-revision-id="2">
				<summary class="trfc161__question-wrapper">
					<b class="trfc161__question">What distinguishes Shin from other Supreme Kais in Dragon Ball Z?</b>
						<img class="trfc161__question-chevron" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/835ea5d8-5dd9-4dc6-83dc-8554b30552d7" alt="toggle section">
				</summary>
				<div class="trfc161__answer">
					<div class="quick-answers__answer-text">
						In Dragon Ball Z, Shin, known as the Supreme Kai, distinguishes himself by ruling the east quadrant of the universe and becoming the primary ruler of Universe 7 following the deaths of the other Supreme Kais. Notably, Shin fights alongside the Z Fighters and can fuse with his bodyguard Kibito to form Kibito Kai. This fusion is reversed in Dragon Ball Super after a wish to Porunga.
					</div>
					<div class="trfc161__answer-source">
						Provided by: Fandom
					</div>
					<div class="quick_answers__report-module-root" data-reportable="1"></div>
				</div>
			</details>
	</div>
</section>
