ame":"What distinguishes Shin from other Supreme Kais in Dragon Ball Z?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Dragon Ball Z, Shin, known as the Supreme Kai, distinguishes himself by ruling the east quadrant of the universe and becoming the primary ruler of Universe 7 following the deaths of the other Supreme Kais. Notably, Shin fights alongside the Z Fighters and can fuse with his bodyguard Kibito to form Kibito Kai. This fusion is reversed in Dragon Ball Super after a wish to Porunga."}}]}</script>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Appearance">Appearance</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D1&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<p>Shin is a short, pink-skinned (light purple in <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z" title="Dragon Ball Z">Dragon Ball Z</a> and <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Super_(anime)" title="Dragon Ball Super (anime)">Dragon Ball Super</a>) Glind with a white mohawk and no other hair. In <i>Z</i> and <i>Super</i>, he wears a long dark teal (dark blue in the <i>Z</i> anime) asymmetrical coat with red lining and pointed shoulder pads, a short orange waist cloak, a light teal long-sleeved shirt with puffy shoulders, light teal pants and red boots. He also wears a pair of green <a href="/wiki/Potara" title="Potara">Potara</a> earrings (yellow in the anime).
</p><p>In <i>Daima</i>, his skin becomes pink to match his manga counterpart and he wears a teal and gold coat, a sky blue waist cloak, a light purple shirt and pants, and white boots.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Personality">Personality</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D2&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<p>Shin's attitude changes throughout the <a href="/wiki/Buu_Saga" title="Buu Saga">Buu Saga</a>. When he is first introduced, he squints his eyes at <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a> and smiles in a manner that makes him seem mysterious and powerful. Just as what a supreme leader of the <a href="/wiki/Universe_7" title="Universe 7">universe</a> should be, he is calm, wise, humble and thinks rationally at critical moments. Later on, his constant surprise at the <a href="/wiki/Saiyan" title="Saiyan">Saiyans</a>' power and his dependence on others to protect the universe against <a href="/wiki/Innocent_Buu" title="Innocent Buu">Majin Buu</a> make him seem more fearful and innocent, most likely due to his previous inability to combat those kinds of powerful beings himself.
</p><p>Although Shin knows a good amount of information about the universe, he is rather ignorant of some important things known by other Kais and <a href="/wiki/God_of_Destruction" title="God of Destruction">Gods of Destruction</a>, due to his lack of full training since the elimination of the other Supreme Kais; for example, he was completely unaware of <a href="/wiki/Zeno" title="Zeno">Zeno</a> and who he was, as in the <a href="/wiki/Tournament_of_Destroyers" title="Tournament of Destroyers">Tournament of Destroyers</a>, he asked his <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">ancestor</a> who he was, for which he was slapped on the head and informed. Adding onto this, he was unaware of <a href="/wiki/Autonomous_Ultra_Instinct_(ability)" title="Autonomous Ultra Instinct (ability)">Ultra Instinct</a>, while many of the other Gods of Destruction and Supreme Kais were familiar with the ability. Yet another example was his obliviousness about the fusing abilities of the <a href="/wiki/Potara" title="Potara">Potara</a>, which led to him fusing with <a href="/wiki/Kibito" title="Kibito">Kibito</a> before realizing the fusion would be permanent.
</p><p>Additionally, Shin shows ignorance of much of information on the rest of the universe. He was completely unaware of the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_(object)" title="Dragon Ball (object)">Dragon Balls</a>, with which Old Kai was much more familiar. He did not know about <a href="/wiki/Super_Saiyan" title="Super Saiyan">Super Saiyans</a> nor many of the events that had transpired throughout the series and was quite shocked to see Goku, <a href="/wiki/Vegeta" title="Vegeta">Vegeta</a> and <a href="/wiki/Gohan" title="Gohan">Gohan</a> overpower, and dispose of the <a href="/wiki/Pui_Pui" title="Pui Pui">same</a> <a href="/wiki/Yakon" title="Yakon">minions</a> of <a href="/wiki/Babidi" title="Babidi">Babidi</a> he himself had greatly feared. In addition, despite prioritizing the safety of the universe, he had remained quite insensitive to the Saiyans' own ambitions and lust for battle and was surprised when Vegeta momentarily <a href="/wiki/Manipulation_Sorcery" title="Manipulation Sorcery">fell</a> in with Babidi to fight Goku and did not care about the threat of Majin Buu at all. He was furthermore shocked when Goku had <a href="/wiki/Suspended_Blast" title="Suspended Blast">threatened</a> to obliterate him on the spot for getting in the way of his and Vegeta's showdown, but he had eventually shared a mutual apology with Goku.
</p><p>Originally, Shin also appeared to have a rather dogmatic and narrow-minded view of good and evil, perhaps as a result of his past trauma dealing with Majin Buu and the deaths of his fellow Kais, he firmly held an almost naive black and white mentality towards those who had lived bad lives. These views gradually began to shift and change over the course of the series as he witnesses Goku and his ability to change the hearts and minds of several <a href="/wiki/Vegeta" title="Vegeta">of</a> <a href="/wiki/Android_18" title="Android 18">his</a> <a href="/wiki/Good_Buu" title="Good Buu">enemies</a> in the past leading him to realize that things were not always as simple as he had initially believed, and that redemption was indeed possible for those who genuinely choose to seek it out.
</p><p>Generally, Shin believes that Supreme Kais must uphold a strict moral standard or at the very least that they should maintain the illusion of said standards. He holds some disgust for perversion, as seen when Goku had offered <a href="/wiki/Dirty_Magazine" title="Dirty Magazine">dirty magazines</a> to Old Kai in exchange for <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai%27s_Unlock_Ability" title="Old Kai's Unlock Ability">unlocking</a> Gohan's power, Shin tells Goku that such an offer was inappropriate, only to be extremely shocked and disgusted when he learns that Old Kai actually uses his <a href="/wiki/Far-Seeing_Arts" title="Far-Seeing Arts">omniscient vision</a> to see girls playing volleyball on the beach, yelling "you call yourself a Kai?!". In the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Super_(manga)" title="Dragon Ball Super (manga)"><i>Dragon Ball Super</i> manga</a>, Shin condemns <a href="/wiki/Goku_Black" title="Goku Black">Goku Black</a> for engaging in behavior unbecoming of a Supreme Kai after the latter <a href="/wiki/Violent_Fierce_God_Slicer" title="Violent Fierce God Slicer">mortally wounds</a> <a href="/wiki/Gowasu" title="Gowasu">Gowasu</a>.
</p><p>Shin has a strained relationship with <a href="/wiki/Beerus" title="Beerus">Beerus</a>, as he rarely gets along with him though he tolerates his occasional rough and rude behavior towards him. Their relationship is further strained after the <a href="/wiki/Grand_Minister" title="Grand Minister">Grand Minister</a> had announced the stipulations for the <a href="/wiki/Tournament_of_Power" title="Tournament of Power">Tournament of Power</a>; after Beerus had condemned him for being too uninvolved with the mortal worlds since Shin believed that <a href="/wiki/Human" title="Human">mortals</a> needed to develop their levels on their own, Shin had retorted to Beerus about him slacking off instead of doing his job.
</p><p>Despite clashing ideals with his power-hungry and sadistic siblings, Shin is still able to be somewhat amiable with them, even having an almost friendly conversation with <a href="/wiki/Dr._Arinsu" title="Dr. Arinsu">Arinsu</a> before their differences ultimately force their groups to fight. He also has a surprisingly friendly relationship with <a href="/wiki/Panzy" title="Panzy">Panzy</a>, taking on a protective older brother–like relationship with her.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Biography">Biography</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D3&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Background">Background</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D4&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>Shin was given the name Nahare at birth and resided on planet <a href="/wiki/Kaishin_(Demon_Realm)" title="Kaishin (Demon Realm)">Kaishin</a> in the <a href="/wiki/Second_Demon_World" title="Second Demon World">Second Demon World</a> as part of the <a href="/wiki/Glind" title="Glind">Glind</a> race.<sup id="cite_ref-DBDep3_2-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-DBDep3-2"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-DBDep7_5-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-DBDep7-5"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> He has two siblings, his older sister <a href="/wiki/Dr._Arinsu" title="Dr. Arinsu">Dr. Arinsu</a> and their younger brother <a href="/wiki/Degesu" title="Degesu">Degesu</a>.
</p><p>At some point, Shin left the <a href="/wiki/Demon_Realm" title="Demon Realm">Demon Realm</a> and migrated to the planet <a href="/wiki/Kaishin" title="Kaishin">Kaishin</a> in <a href="/wiki/Universe_7" title="Universe 7">Universe 7</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-DBDep2_6-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-DBDep2-6"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Prior to having become a Supreme Kai, Shin had been an apprentice to the old Supreme Kai.<sup id="cite_ref-7" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-7"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 170px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/0e/EastSupKaiReads.png/revision/latest?cb=20101122222608" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin as the East Supreme Kai during the peaceful era." src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="170" height="128" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="EastSupKaiReads.png" data-image-key="EastSupKaiReads.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/0e/EastSupKaiReads.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/170?cb=20101122222608"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/0e/EastSupKaiReads.png/revision/latest?cb=20101122222608" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin as the East Supreme Kai during the peaceful era." src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/0e/EastSupKaiReads.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/170?cb=20101122222608" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="170" height="128" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="EastSupKaiReads.png" data-image-key="EastSupKaiReads.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/0e/EastSupKaiReads.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/170?cb=20101122222608"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:EastSupKaiReads.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin as the East Supreme Kai during the peaceful era.</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Enjoying a peaceful life on the <a href="/wiki/Sacred_World_of_the_Kai" title="Sacred World of the Kai">Sacred World of the Kai</a> with his fellow <a href="/wiki/Supreme_Kai_(position)" title="Supreme Kai (position)">Supreme Kais</a>, Shin was unaware until too late that he and the other Supreme Kais had been targeted and marked for death by the ruthless wizard <a href="/wiki/Bibidi" title="Bibidi">Bibidi</a>, who was determined to wipe them out by unleashing his fearsome monster, <a href="/wiki/Kid_Buu" title="Kid Buu">Majin Buu</a>, on all of them.
</p><p>After hearing that <a href="/wiki/North_Supreme_Kai" title="North Supreme Kai">North</a> and <a href="/wiki/West_Supreme_Kai" title="West Supreme Kai">West Supreme Kais</a> had been killed by Kid Buu, Shin and <a href="/wiki/Grand_Supreme_Kai" title="Grand Supreme Kai">Grand Supreme Kai</a> prepared to face off against the buffed-up monster (Kid Buu who had <a href="/wiki/Absorption" title="Absorption">absorbed</a> <a href="/wiki/South_Supreme_Kai" title="South Supreme Kai">South Supreme Kai</a> and transformed into what <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">Old Kai</a> later called the <a href="/wiki/Kid_Buu#Abilties" title="Kid Buu">huge Buu</a>, or in the games and by anime known as Super Buu). While Huge Buu was after Shin, Grand Supreme Kai intervened but was absorbed by Huge Buu. But Huge Buu turned into an <a href="/wiki/Innocent_Buu" title="Innocent Buu">obese, childlike monster</a>, and to his relief, Shin was spared by Majin Buu, whose evil had been reduced thanks to Grand Supreme Kai's good nature.<sup id="cite_ref-8" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-8"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>To avenge his friends, Shin eventually caught Bibidi off guard and destroyed the evil wizard while Majin Buu was <a href="/wiki/Sealed_Ball" title="Sealed Ball">locked up in a ball</a>. Shin then hid the ball deep under the surface of <a href="/wiki/Earth" title="Earth">Earth</a>, fearing that he would be powerless to stop Majin Buu himself.
</p><p>Shin then returned to the Sacred World of the Kai, aided by a new bodyguard, <a href="/wiki/Kibito" title="Kibito">Kibito</a>, to carry on with his life of peace.
</p><p>He eventually become a full-fledged Supreme Kai at some point after the <a href="/wiki/All_Universe_Hide_and_Seek_Tournament" title="All Universe Hide and Seek Tournament">All Universe Hide and Seek Tournament</a>, which occurred during or after <a href="/wiki/239,856_Before_Age" title="239,856 Before Age">239,856 Before Age</a>. Due to the deaths of the other four Supreme Kais, Shin became known simply as <i>the</i> Supreme Kai.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Dragon_Ball_Z"><i>Dragon Ball Z</i></span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D5&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Majin_Buu_Saga">Majin Buu Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D6&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main articles: <a href="/wiki/World_Tournament_Saga" title="World Tournament Saga">World Tournament Saga</a>, <a href="/wiki/Babidi_Saga" title="Babidi Saga">Babidi Saga</a>, <a href="/wiki/Majin_Buu_Saga" title="Majin Buu Saga">Majin Buu Saga</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Fusion_Saga" title="Fusion Saga">Fusion Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/5/54/SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png/revision/latest?cb=20100424143927" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Kibito making their debut in Dragon Ball Z" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="267" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png" data-image-key="SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/5/54/SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100424143927"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/5/54/SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png/revision/latest?cb=20100424143927" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Kibito making their debut in Dragon Ball Z" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/5/54/SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100424143927" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="267" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png" data-image-key="SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/5/54/SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100424143927"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:SupremeKaiKibitoWMATNV.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin and Kibito making their debut in <i>Dragon Ball Z</i></p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Many eons later, Shin and Kibito traveled to Earth to find the help of Earth's greatest heroes, <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a>, <a href="/wiki/Gohan" title="Gohan">Gohan</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Vegeta" title="Vegeta">Vegeta</a>, for he had learned that <a href="/wiki/Babidi" title="Babidi">Babidi</a> (the clone of Bibidi) was planning to release Majin Buu from a <a href="/wiki/Sealed_Ball" title="Sealed Ball">Sealed Ball</a>. Babidi had sent two of his possessed human henchmen, <a href="/wiki/Yamu" title="Yamu">Yamu</a> and <a href="/wiki/Spopovich" title="Spopovich">Spopovich</a>, to start gathering energy for Majin Buu, and the pair did so starting with the <a href="/wiki/25th_World_Martial_Arts_Tournament" class="mw-redirect" title="25th World Martial Arts Tournament">25th World Martial Arts Tournament</a>. Shin paralyzed Gohan, and after Yamu and Spopovich succeeded in <a href="/wiki/Majin_Buu_Resurrection" title="Majin Buu Resurrection">stealing Gohan's energy</a>, Shin explains he paralyzed Gohan so they could get the energy so he could follow them. They proceeded to head back to <a href="/wiki/Babidi%27s_Spaceship" title="Babidi's Spaceship">Babidi's Spaceship</a>, with Shin and some of the Z-Fighters following them. When they arrived, Shin was shocked to see that Babidi had already enlisted the aid of the Demon King, <a href="/wiki/Dabura" title="Dabura">Dabura</a>. Much to Shin's horror, Dabura had easily discovered the Kais' and the Z Fighters' hiding grounds, and proceeded to attack everyone, killing Kibito in the process and turning <a href="/wiki/Piccolo" title="Piccolo">Piccolo</a> and <a href="/wiki/Krillin" title="Krillin">Krillin</a> to stone with <a href="/wiki/Stone_Spit" title="Stone Spit">his spit</a>. Shin eventually entered Babidi's ship along with the three Saiyans to go through multiple stage battles in order to reach the heart of Babidi's ship where the dormant Majin Buu would be found. Shin warned everyone that Babidi's minions were considered as the strongest fighters in the universe, and it was recommended that each of them should fight together. However, Shin was often left in disbelief by how easily the Saiyans defeated these would-be strongest fighters with ease and by themselves (with the likes of Vegeta defeating <a href="/wiki/Pui_Pui" title="Pui Pui">Pui Pui</a> and Goku defeating <a href="/wiki/Yakon" title="Yakon">Yakon</a>).
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/2/26/East-supreme-kai.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20090125155627" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin at the World Martial Arts Tournament" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="144" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="East-supreme-kai.jpg" data-image-key="East-supreme-kai.jpg" data-relevant="0" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/2/26/East-supreme-kai.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20090125155627"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/2/26/East-supreme-kai.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20090125155627" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin at the World Martial Arts Tournament" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/2/26/East-supreme-kai.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20090125155627" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="144" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="East-supreme-kai.jpg" data-image-key="East-supreme-kai.jpg" data-relevant="0" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/2/26/East-supreme-kai.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20090125155627"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:East-supreme-kai.jpg" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin at the World Martial Arts Tournament</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>When it came time for Gohan to fight, his opponent was Dabura and Gohan was able to hold his own. After Vegeta expressed his outrage to Gohan's poor fighting, saying he should have beaten him by then, Dabura mysteriously decided to withdraw from his battle with Gohan. Dabura stated that he has discovered the perfect warrior to handle them all at once, which is a revelation that baffles Shin, believing that Babidi does not have anyone more powerful than Dabura. After a heated argument with Vegeta (who threatened to destroy the ship with the risk of awakening Majin Buu), Shin was quick to realize that Vegeta is the warrior that Dabura spoke of, and his fears came to light when Babidi had <a href="/wiki/Manipulation_Sorcery" title="Manipulation Sorcery">possessed</a> Vegeta, turning him into Majin Vegeta.
</p>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/19/GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png/revision/latest?cb=20140601162943" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin's life put on the line" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="99" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png" data-image-key="GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/19/GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20140601162943"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/19/GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png/revision/latest?cb=20140601162943" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin's life put on the line" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/19/GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20140601162943" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="99" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png" data-image-key="GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/19/GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20140601162943"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:GokuThreatensSupremeKai.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin's life put on the line</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Babidi transports them all back to the World Martial Arts Tournament, and Majin Vegeta begins to kill many civilians (and almost his own wife, <a href="/wiki/Bulma" title="Bulma">Bulma</a>) with a couple of <a href="/wiki/Big_Bang_Attack" title="Big Bang Attack">Big Bang Attacks</a>. When it became clear that Majin Vegeta will proceed to kill unless Goku accepts his challenge to the finish, Goku is forced to accept the challenge provided that they are transported by Babidi to an area with no civilians present. Shin, realizing that the ensuing clash between the Saiyans will provide Babidi with enough energy to resurrect Majin Buu in full, steps in between Goku and Majin Vegeta, demanding the former stand down. To everyone's surprise, however, Goku extends his hand, generating a <a href="/wiki/Suspended_Blast" title="Suspended Blast"><i>ki</i> blast and holding it in front of Shin to threaten him into submission</a>. Completely at risk of being destroyed and seeing that Goku and Vegeta are far too powerful to stop, Shin had no choice but to relent and let the battle transpire, though Goku apologizes to him for threatening him so. After Babidi fulfills Goku's request to be transported to a deserted area, Shin accompanied by Gohan, managed to reach the heart of Babidi's ship where the cocoon of Majin Buu is located. Shin and Gohan are greeted by Babidi and Dabura who are trying to prevent any interruption of Majin Buu's return.
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d6/KaioshinAtMPlanet.png/revision/latest?cb=20110305213455" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin fearing Majin Buu's revival" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="KaioshinAtMPlanet.png" data-image-key="KaioshinAtMPlanet.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d6/KaioshinAtMPlanet.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20110305213455"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d6/KaioshinAtMPlanet.png/revision/latest?cb=20110305213455" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin fearing Majin Buu's revival" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d6/KaioshinAtMPlanet.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20110305213455" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="KaioshinAtMPlanet.png" data-image-key="KaioshinAtMPlanet.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d6/KaioshinAtMPlanet.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20110305213455"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:KaioshinAtMPlanet.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin fearing Majin Buu's revival</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>As Shin and Gohan prepare their assault, <a href="/wiki/Innocent_Buu" title="Innocent Buu">Majin Buu</a> had already reached full power as a result of Goku and Majin Vegeta fighting as <a href="/wiki/Super_Saiyan_2" title="Super Saiyan 2">Super Saiyan 2s</a>, giving Majin Buu a massive boost in power. Despite Gohan's best efforts in stopping Majin Buu's revival with <a href="/wiki/Kamehameha" title="Kamehameha">Kamehameha</a> waves, it was not enough and Majin Buu had returned. Shin and Gohan witnessed in horror as Majin Buu easily overwhelmed Demon King Dabura in battle (with Majin Buu angered after being badly criticized by Dabura as an "idiot and a waste" due to Majin Buu's childlike attitude) and Babidi takes temporary control of Majin Buu by threatening to seal him up in the very same ball just like his father did eons before. Babidi ordered his new "pet" to kill Shin and Gohan. Shin and Gohan were far outmatched by Majin Buu's fighting abilities. Majin Buu had severely and almost fatally injured Shin in battle and had nearly killed Gohan by attempting to blast him into outer space. With the little strength he had left, Shin nullified Buu's attack over Gohan thus saving Gohan's life. Buu was later confronted by Majin Vegeta who had already rendered Goku unconscious during their battle. Majin Vegeta challenged Buu to the death to not only redeem himself for the suffering he has caused before but to also avenge Gohan, believing that he is dead because he can no longer feel his presence. Majin Vegeta could not stop Majin Buu despite utilizing a self-explosion technique to finish Buu. Shin had survived his ordeal with Buu once again but was still badly injured and weak. While trying to find Gohan, Shin had collapsed and lost consciousness.
</p>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/8a/GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png/revision/latest?cb=20100514160815" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Supreme Kai and Kibito introduce Gohan to the Z Sword" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png" data-image-key="GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/8a/GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100514160815"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/8a/GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png/revision/latest?cb=20100514160815" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Supreme Kai and Kibito introduce Gohan to the Z Sword" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/8a/GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100514160815" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png" data-image-key="GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/8a/GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100514160815"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:GohanKibitoSupremeKaiZSword.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Supreme Kai and Kibito introduce Gohan to the Z Sword</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Fortunately, Kibito (who was resurrected by <a href="/wiki/Shenron" title="Shenron">Shenron</a> via <a href="/wiki/Bulma" title="Bulma">Bulma</a>'s wish to restore the lives of the good people killed within that day) found Shin and healed him. Then, the two found and healed Gohan, and <a href="/wiki/Kai_Kai" title="Kai Kai">teleport</a> him to the World of the Kais. There, they would have him unlock the legendary <a href="/wiki/Z_Sword" title="Z Sword">Z Sword</a> and try and use it to help him defeat Majin Buu once and for all. During Gohan's training, Goku, whose time on Earth had ended (he was dead, due to sacrificing himself to stop <a href="/wiki/Cell" title="Cell">Cell</a> seven years earlier) arrived on the World of the Kais. After Gohan had mastered the handling of the unbelievably heavy Z Sword, Shin thought that a proper demonstration of the sword's power was in order. He materialized a block of <a href="/wiki/Katchin" title="Katchin">Katchin</a>, the hardest known metal in the universe for Gohan to cut through with the Z Sword. However, the Z Sword was broken from the demonstration (with Goku throwing it at Gohan to slice with the sword) which caused the release of <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">Old Kai</a>, who was an ancestor of Shin.
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/ff/SupremeKaiSitting.png/revision/latest?cb=20120124071755" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin sitting in the Sacred World of Kai" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="94" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="SupremeKaiSitting.png" data-image-key="SupremeKaiSitting.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/ff/SupremeKaiSitting.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20120124071755"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/ff/SupremeKaiSitting.png/revision/latest?cb=20120124071755" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin sitting in the Sacred World of Kai" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/ff/SupremeKaiSitting.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20120124071755" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="94" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="SupremeKaiSitting.png" data-image-key="SupremeKaiSitting.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/ff/SupremeKaiSitting.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20120124071755"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:SupremeKaiSitting.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin sitting in the Sacred World of Kai</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Shin, along with Goku and Kibito, witnessed the elder Kai train Gohan personally, awakening Gohan's hidden sleeping powers (as this is apparently a technique that the Elder Kai's enemies had feared). During this time, everyone could sense that Majin Buu had transformed into Super Buu and had exterminated the planet's populace with <a href="/wiki/Human_Extinction_Attack" title="Human Extinction Attack">Human Extinction Attack</a>. When <a href="/wiki/Gotenks" title="Gotenks">Gotenks</a> could not stop <a href="/wiki/Super_Buu" title="Super Buu">Super Buu</a>, Gohan returned to Earth and was able to best Super Buu in battle, until being absorbed.
</p>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/86/KibitoKai.png/revision/latest?cb=20091113183547" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Kibito unknowingly fuse and form Kibito Kai" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="KibitoKai.png" data-image-key="KibitoKai.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/86/KibitoKai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20091113183547"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/86/KibitoKai.png/revision/latest?cb=20091113183547" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Kibito unknowingly fuse and form Kibito Kai" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/86/KibitoKai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20091113183547" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="KibitoKai.png" data-image-key="KibitoKai.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/86/KibitoKai.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20091113183547"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:KibitoKai.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin and Kibito unknowingly fuse and form Kibito Kai</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure> 
<p>Old Kai had revealed that the Potara Earrings can perform fusion between two beings with one person wearing just one earring on the left ear and the other person wears one earring on the right. Shin and Kibito tested Elder Kai's revelations (and were oblivious to the fact that the fusion was permanent until it was too late) and became <a href="/wiki/Kibito_Kai" title="Kibito Kai">Kibito Kai</a>. Although Kibito Kai was much stronger than Shin, his power was still insufficient to defeat Majin Buu. After becoming aware of the permanent fusion, Goku (resurrected by Old Kai's life-force) returned to Earth to attempt to fuse with his son Gohan, who was being outclassed by the much more powerful Super Buu (who had already absorbed Piccolo and Gotenks). Shin's personality was dominant in Kibito Kai, with no notable traces of Kibito.
</p><p>Kibito Kai's later roles no longer required direct battle against villains, only interference on Goku's behalf with the use of his <a href="/wiki/Kai_Kai" title="Kai Kai">Kai Kai</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Dragon_Ball_Daima"><i>Dragon Ball Daima</i></span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D7&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Daima_Saga">Daima Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D8&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Daima_Saga" title="Daima Saga">Daima Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/6/61/Mini_Shin.png/revision/latest?cb=20240906024748" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin turned back into a child by Gomah's wish" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="168" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Mini Shin.png" data-image-key="Mini_Shin.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/6/61/Mini_Shin.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20240906024748"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/6/61/Mini_Shin.png/revision/latest?cb=20240906024748" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin turned back into a child by Gomah's wish" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/6/61/Mini_Shin.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20240906024748" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="168" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Mini Shin.png" data-image-key="Mini_Shin.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/6/61/Mini_Shin.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20240906024748"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Mini_Shin.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin turned back into a child by Gomah's wish</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Shin and Kibito are at <a href="/wiki/Capsule_Corporation" title="Capsule Corporation">Capsule Corporation</a> celebrating <a href="/wiki/Trunks" title="Trunks">Trunks</a>' ninth birthday and are noticed by Goku who was surprised they separated from being <a href="/wiki/Kibito_Kai" title="Kibito Kai">Kibito Kai</a>. Shin and Kibito explain that when Goku and <a href="/wiki/Vegeta" title="Vegeta">Vegeta</a> separated from <a href="/wiki/Vegito" title="Vegito">Vegito</a> <a href="/wiki/Inside_Buu" title="Inside Buu">inside Buu</a>'s body, they learnt that <a href="/wiki/Good_Buu" title="Good Buu">Buu</a>'s insides produce a type of gas that can nullify the <a href="/wiki/Potara" title="Potara">Potara</a>'s powers and asked Buu to <a href="/wiki/Absorption" title="Absorption">absorb</a> and spit them out as well. Shin wonders where <a href="/wiki/Gohan" title="Gohan">Gohan</a> is and learns that busy studying. He and Kibito sense a familiar presence when <a href="/wiki/Shenron" title="Shenron">Shenron</a> is summoned and are turned back into children with the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Team" title="Dragon Team">others</a> due to <a href="/wiki/Gomah" title="Gomah">Gomah</a>'s wish.<sup id="cite_ref-9" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-9"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> After the initial shock of realizing what has happened to them, Shin tells Goku of an unpleasant presence that he sensed at <a href="/wiki/The_Lookout" title="The Lookout">the Lookout</a> and they along with Kibito and <a href="/wiki/Piccolo" title="Piccolo">Piccolo</a> head there. When <a href="/wiki/Mr._Popo" title="Mr. Popo">Mr. Popo</a> tells them that <a href="/wiki/Dende" title="Dende">Dende</a> has been kidnapped by individuals from the Demon Realm, with <a href="/wiki/Degesu" title="Degesu">Degesu</a>, Shin's brother, being one of them. 
</p>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4c/DBD_Ep_2_08.png/revision/latest?cb=20241019120153" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin, Goku and Glorio on the way to the Sir Warp" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="DBD Ep 2 08.png" data-image-key="DBD_Ep_2_08.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4c/DBD_Ep_2_08.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241019120153"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4c/DBD_Ep_2_08.png/revision/latest?cb=20241019120153" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin, Goku and Glorio on the way to the Sir Warp" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4c/DBD_Ep_2_08.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241019120153" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="DBD Ep 2 08.png" data-image-key="DBD_Ep_2_08.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4c/DBD_Ep_2_08.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241019120153"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:DBD_Ep_2_08.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin, Goku and Glorio on the way to the Sir Warp</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Shin commands Kibito to fetch their <a href="/wiki/Demon_Realm_Plane" title="Demon Realm Plane">spaceship</a> back on the <a href="/wiki/Sacred_World_of_the_Kai" title="Sacred World of the Kai">Sacred World of the Kai</a>. However, after Kibito quickly teleports there and back with the ship, Shin looks it over and realizes it will no longer turn on due to being neglected for so long. Goku suggests getting Bulma to help fix the ship and while she works on it, Shin and Kibito explain to Vegeta about the workings of the Demon Realm. Later that night, Glorio appears before them and takes Goku and Shin with him back to Demon Realm to defeat Gomah.<sup id="cite_ref-DBDep2_6-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-DBDep2-6"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Upon reaching <a href="/wiki/Sir_Warp" title="Sir Warp">Sir Warp</a>, Shin disguises Goku's ears in order for him to be passed off as a <a href="/wiki/Demon" title="Demon">Demon</a> and Glorio gives the appropriate pin number, the trio are whisked away though unfortunately Shin is not able to <a href="/wiki/Telepathy" title="Telepathy">contact</a> Kibito in time to give him the pin number. After reaching the <a href="/wiki/Third_Demon_World" title="Third Demon World">Third Demon World</a>, they arrive at a hotel to stay and get into a fight with locals due to seeing Goku's rounded ears. In the morning, their plane gets stolen<sup id="cite_ref-DBDep3_2-2" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-DBDep3-2"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and travel on foot until they reach the tea shop where Glorio buys a <a href="/wiki/Sky_Seed" title="Sky Seed">Sky Seed</a> to travel in the air with until it almost lands in the <a href="/wiki/Sea_of_Darkness" title="Sea of Darkness">Sea of Darkness</a>.
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/f3/DBD_Ep5_01.png/revision/latest?cb=20241111162744" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Goku meet Panzy" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="DBD Ep5 01.png" data-image-key="DBD_Ep5_01.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/f3/DBD_Ep5_01.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241111162744"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/f3/DBD_Ep5_01.png/revision/latest?cb=20241111162744" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Goku meet Panzy" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/f3/DBD_Ep5_01.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241111162744" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="DBD Ep5 01.png" data-image-key="DBD_Ep5_01.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/f/f3/DBD_Ep5_01.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241111162744"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:DBD_Ep5_01.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin and Goku meet Panzy</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>While traveling on foot again to the next town, Shin and Goku learn that the Demon Realm has its <a href="/wiki/Demon_Realm_Dragon_Ball" title="Demon Realm Dragon Ball">own set of Dragon Balls</a> protected by the <a href="/wiki/Tamagami" title="Tamagami">Tamagami</a>. Once reaching town, Shin, Goku, and Glorio notice the <a href="/wiki/Gendarmerie" title="Gendarmerie">Gendarmerie</a> collecting taxes and lifespan from the locals until a <a href="/wiki/Panzy" title="Panzy">Masked Majin</a> intervenes. Once Goku steps in to help the Majin, they are forced to escape and Panzy removes her mask to introduce herself.<sup id="cite_ref-10" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-10"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The three begin to head off with Goku accidentally letting slip that they are on the way to <a href="/wiki/Kadan_Castle" title="Kadan Castle">Kadan Castle</a> and so Panzy invites herself along, revealing to be the Princess and daughter of King <a href="/wiki/Kadan" title="Kadan">Kadan</a> once they reach the castle. Heading inside, they meet with the King who becomes annoyed that Glorio has merely brought along children when he had been promised warriors strong enough to have defeated the great <a href="/wiki/Kid_Buu" title="Kid Buu">Majin Buu</a>. However, once Goku shows his strength against Kadan's soldiers, they are given supplies to help them on their journey with Panzy even joining them.<sup id="cite_ref-11" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-11"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/81/Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png/revision/latest?cb=20241123011054" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin removes Panzy's collar" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Pan Paka Paan 3.png" data-image-key="Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/81/Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241123011054"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/81/Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png/revision/latest?cb=20241123011054" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin removes Panzy's collar" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/81/Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241123011054" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Pan Paka Paan 3.png" data-image-key="Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/81/Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241123011054"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Pan_Paka_Paan_3.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin removes Panzy's collar</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>On their way to their next destination, they are stopped by the Gendarmerie who are in search of Goku. When they try to take Panzy away, Shin along with Glorio and Goku defeat them. Panzy realizes that the Gendarmerie will be able to keep track of their location from that point onwards due to them having scanned the <a href="/wiki/Magic_Collar" title="Magic Collar">collar</a> around her neck. Using his abilities, Shin chants the words "<a href="/wiki/Pan_Paka_Paan" title="Pan Paka Paan">Pan Paka Paan</a>" which causes the collar to shatter and fall away, freeing Panzy. Grateful, Panzy asks Shin for his real name which is "Nahare". Goku decides to call him by that name from now on but after using it just the once prefers to keep calling him Supreme Kai and they continue their journey towards <a href="/wiki/Tamagami_Number_Three" title="Tamagami Number Three">Tamagami Number Three</a>. Goku encounters and challenges Tamagami Number Three for the right to earn its Dragon Ball<sup id="cite_ref-DBDep7_5-2" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-DBDep7-5"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and eventually prevails.<sup id="cite_ref-12" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-12"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>After an overnight stay at a hotel,<sup id="cite_ref-13" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-13"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> the group arrive at the Sir Warp where they proceed to enter into the <a href="/wiki/Second_Demon_World" title="Second Demon World">Second Demon World</a>. After another run in with the Gendarmerie and a <a href="/wiki/Kraken" title="Kraken">Kraken</a>, the four land on the planet <a href="/wiki/Namek_(Demon_Realm)" title="Namek (Demon Realm)">Namek of the Demon Realm</a>. Having also now entered the Second Demon World, Goku fetches Vegeta, Piccolo, Bulma and <a href="/wiki/Hybis" title="Hybis">Hybis</a> and brings them over to the others. Whilst still on Namek, Shin explains some of the history of the <a href="/wiki/Multiverse" title="Multiverse">Multiverse</a>, the Demon Realm and his own past. Being a <a href="/wiki/Glind" title="Glind">Glind</a> that was born from one of the five, now extinct, <a href="/wiki/Glind_Tree" title="Glind Tree">Glind Trees</a>, Shin revolted along with many of his kind during <a href="/wiki/Abura" title="Abura">Abura</a>'s tyrannical rule, leaving the Demon Realm to move to the planet <a href="/wiki/Kaishin" title="Kaishin">Kaishin</a> where he was eventually appointed the position of <a href="/wiki/Supreme_Kai_(position)" title="Supreme Kai (position)">Supreme Kai</a> by <a href="/wiki/Rymus" title="Rymus">Rymus</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-14" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-14"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/95/DBD_12_08.png/revision/latest?cb=20241228161624" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin watches Vegeta fight" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="DBD 12 08.png" data-image-key="DBD_12_08.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/95/DBD_12_08.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241228161624"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/95/DBD_12_08.png/revision/latest?cb=20241228161624" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin watches Vegeta fight" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/95/DBD_12_08.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241228161624" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="DBD 12 08.png" data-image-key="DBD_12_08.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/95/DBD_12_08.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241228161624"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:DBD_12_08.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin watches Vegeta fight</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>The now expanded group continue on their way, now also joined by the elderly Namekian <a href="/wiki/Neva" title="Neva">Neva</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-15" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-15"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> After Vegeta succeeds in obtaining the second Dragon Ball from <a href="/wiki/Tamagami_Number_Two" title="Tamagami Number Two">Tamagami Number Two</a><sup id="cite_ref-16" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-16"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and then making an unexpected landing on the planet <a href="/wiki/Mega" title="Mega">Mega</a>,<sup id="cite_ref-17" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-17"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> they arrive at the entrance to the <a href="/wiki/Demon_Realm_Tunnel" title="Demon Realm Tunnel">Demon Realm Tunnel</a> with Neva removing the barrier surrounding it. They make their way into the <a href="/wiki/First_Demon_World" title="First Demon World">First Demon World</a> where they immediately attacked by the Gendarmerie<sup id="cite_ref-18" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-18"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-19" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-19"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> but eventually make their way to the <a href="/wiki/Demon%27s_King_Palace" title="Demon's King Palace">Demon's King Palace</a> where Shin confronts his brother who is holding Dende at hostage. They are able to save Dende and Degesu is captured and taken away.
</p>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ea/DBD_17_01.png/revision/latest?cb=20250212225119" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin greets his sister" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="DBD 17 01.png" data-image-key="DBD_17_01.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ea/DBD_17_01.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20250212225119"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ea/DBD_17_01.png/revision/latest?cb=20250212225119" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin greets his sister" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ea/DBD_17_01.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20250212225119" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="DBD 17 01.png" data-image-key="DBD_17_01.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ea/DBD_17_01.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20250212225119"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:DBD_17_01.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin greets his sister</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>After heading outside, they make their way to the courtyard in order to face <a href="/wiki/Tamagami_Number_One" title="Tamagami Number One">Tamagami Number One</a> only to instead come face to face with Shin's sister, <a href="/wiki/Dr._Arinsu" title="Dr. Arinsu">Dr. Arinsu</a> who is in possession of the last Dragon Ball.<sup id="cite_ref-20" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-20"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Shortly afterwards Gomah emerges from his palace having obtained the <a href="/wiki/Evil_Third_Eye" title="Evil Third Eye">Evil Third Eye</a> and wanting to test his powers. Shin joins the others in combating him,<sup id="cite_ref-21" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-21"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> but his strength proves to be too much for the Supreme Kai to handle and resorted to mostly watching from the sidelines. In the end though, Glorio gathers the three Dragon Balls<sup id="cite_ref-22" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-22"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and wishes for everyone to be restored to their rightful age<sup id="cite_ref-23" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-23"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and Gomah is defeated and sealed away along with Degesu.
</p><p>With Gomah and Degesu out of the picture, Arinsu asks who the next Supreme Demon King should be. Shin suggests Arinsu should take the role, but she declines and <a href="/wiki/Majin_Kuu" title="Majin Kuu">Majin Kuu</a> takes the position having been the one to defeat Gomah. Shin and the others return to the Third Demon World where they obtain some supplies and make their farewells before heading off back to the <a href="/wiki/Universe_7" title="Universe 7">Outside World</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-24" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-24"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Dragon_Ball_Super"><i>Dragon Ball Super</i></span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D9&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="God_of_Destruction_Beerus_Saga">God of Destruction Beerus Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D10&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/God_of_Destruction_Beerus_Saga" title="God of Destruction Beerus Saga">God of Destruction Beerus Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/82/Shin_and_Kibito.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20171119184532" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Kibito used the Namekian Dragon Balls to defuse" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="122" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Shin and Kibito.jpg" data-image-key="Shin_and_Kibito.jpg" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/82/Shin_and_Kibito.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20171119184532"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/82/Shin_and_Kibito.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20171119184532" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin and Kibito used the Namekian Dragon Balls to defuse" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/82/Shin_and_Kibito.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20171119184532" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="122" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Shin and Kibito.jpg" data-image-key="Shin_and_Kibito.jpg" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/82/Shin_and_Kibito.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20171119184532"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Shin_and_Kibito.jpg" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin and Kibito used the Namekian Dragon Balls to defuse</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>In manga chapter "<a href="/wiki/Battle_of_Gods_(manga_chapter)" title="Battle of Gods (manga chapter)">Battle of Gods</a>", Kibito Kai gathers the Namekian Dragon Balls to get them out of Champa's grasp, only to find that they were not what he was looking for. Kibito Kai then uses their Dragon Balls to wish himself back into Shin and Kibito. As a result, Shin is no longer permanently fused with Kibito.
</p>
<div style="clear: both;"></div>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Universe_6_Saga">Universe 6 Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D11&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Universe_6_Saga" title="Universe 6 Saga">Universe 6 Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-right show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/15/Universe6-7Kaioshin.png/revision/latest?cb=20160222065941" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin, Kibito and Old Kai arrive on the Nameless Planet" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Universe6-7Kaioshin.png" data-image-key="Universe6-7Kaioshin.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/15/Universe6-7Kaioshin.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20160222065941"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/15/Universe6-7Kaioshin.png/revision/latest?cb=20160222065941" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin, Kibito and Old Kai arrive on the Nameless Planet" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/15/Universe6-7Kaioshin.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20160222065941" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Universe6-7Kaioshin.png" data-image-key="Universe6-7Kaioshin.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/15/Universe6-7Kaioshin.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20160222065941"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Universe6-7Kaioshin.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin, Kibito and Old Kai arrive on the Nameless Planet</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>In the anime, sometime after the battle with Golden Frieza, Kibito Kai goes to <a href="/wiki/New_Namek" title="New Namek">New Namek</a> to request to use their <a href="/wiki/Namekian_Dragon_Balls" class="mw-redirect" title="Namekian Dragon Balls">Dragon Balls</a> so they could defuse into Shin and Kibito because he thinks it feels weird. Shin, along with <a href="/wiki/Kibito" title="Kibito">Kibito</a> and <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">Old Kai</a>, attends the tournament between Beerus' and Champa's teams on the <a href="/wiki/Nameless_Planet" title="Nameless Planet">Nameless Planet</a>. When <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a> and the rest of the gang arrives, Shin greets Goku. When he tries to explain to Goku why he and Kibito are split, Goku quickly rushes to <a href="/wiki/Fuwa" title="Fuwa">Fuwa</a> and his <a href="/wiki/Fuwa%27s_Attendant" title="Fuwa's Attendant">attendant</a>. When <a href="/wiki/Zeno" title="Zeno">Zeno</a> appears at the end of the tournament, Shin does not recognize him (being a newer Supreme Kai) and whispers to Old Kai, asking who the "childlike creature" is and earning a punch to the head from the older deity for his gross misunderstanding. After being informed on just how important Zeno is, he joins his fellow gods in bowing at Zeno's feet.
</p>
<h4><span id=".22Future.22_Trunks_Saga"></span><span class="mw-headline" id='"Future"_Trunks_Saga'>"Future" Trunks Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D12&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga" title='"Future" Trunks Saga'>"Future" Trunks Saga</a></div>
<p>In the manga version of <i>Super</i>, Shin and Kibito pay a visit to <a href="/wiki/Universe_10" title="Universe 10">Universe 10</a>, where <a href="/wiki/Zamasu" title="Zamasu">Zamasu</a> and Kibito engage in a sparring match. Shin is shocked and impressed at Zamasu's fighting prowess, witnessing him effortlessly countering every move Kibito makes. After the match, Zamasu praises Shin for his defeat of Majin Buu, but Shin gives the credit to Goku and everyone on Earth, and Zamasu asks who Goku is. Upon hearing that Goku is a Saiyan, Zamasu's comments about him being a "mere mortal" who gained power transcending to the level of God and that unnecessary existences should be eliminated flustered Shin slightly, but he dismisses it as he and Kibito return to their own universe.
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ef/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png/revision/latest?cb=20170612022006" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin, Goku and Whis at Zeno's Palace" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="102" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name='"Future" Trunks Saga - EP55 11.png' data-image-key="%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ef/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20170612022006"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ef/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png/revision/latest?cb=20170612022006" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin, Goku and Whis at Zeno's Palace" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ef/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20170612022006" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="102" class="thumbimage" data-image-name='"Future" Trunks Saga - EP55 11.png' data-image-key="%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/ef/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20170612022006"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga_-_EP55_11.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin, Goku and Whis at Zeno's Palace</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Shin, along with Old Kai and Kibito, is shocked when he hears <a href="/wiki/Zeno" title="Zeno">Zeno</a> has requested Goku's presence. Upon Goku's and Whis's urging, he takes the two of them to <a href="/wiki/Zeno%27s_Palace" title="Zeno's Palace">Zeno's Palace</a>, where he and Whis greet the <a href="/wiki/Grand_Minister" title="Grand Minister">Grand Minister</a> with a bow. After being teleported to Zeno's throne, Shin gets on his knees and bows in respect. When Zeno requests that Goku be his friend, Shin quickly responds for Goku in the affirmative, to which he is silenced by Zeno. He is as equally surprised as <a href="/wiki/Whis" title="Whis">Whis</a> and <a href="/wiki/Zeno%27s_Attendants" title="Zeno's Attendants">Zeno's Attendants</a> upon Goku's nickname of "Zen-chan" and is so distressed Goku has to literally carry him out of the palace. He then teleports himself, Goku, and Whis back to the <a href="/wiki/Sacred_World_of_the_Kai" title="Sacred World of the Kai">Sacred World of the Kai</a>, where he panics upon hearing that Goku did not think about what friend to bring for Zeno before promising him one.
</p><p>Shin later accompanies Goku, Beerus and Whis to Universe 10, learning of Zamasu's plan to kill Gowasu. Upon checking to see that Gowasu has not been threatened, they leave, but actually watch a projected view of them. They eventually witness Zamasu kill Gowasu, and after Whis used <a href="/wiki/Temporal_Do-Over" title="Temporal Do-Over">Temporal Do-Over</a> to undo his death, the Universe 7 group save Gowasu and confront Zamasu. Shin explains Zamasu's plans to a shocked Gowasu. Cornered, Zamasu tries to attack, but he is intercepted and destroyed instantaneously by Beerus.
</p><p>He accompanies Gowasu to the Universe 7 future after being notified of what Goku Black/Present Zamasu did to the alternate timeline in a confrontation with the two versions of Zamasu in their immoral actions. When asked to return to the present both of the Kai's declined saying they would like to see the fight through to the end.
</p>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-right show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/05/The_two_Supreme_Kais.png/revision/latest?cb=20161215183033" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Gowasu and Shin" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="104" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="The two Supreme Kais.png" data-image-key="The_two_Supreme_Kais.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/05/The_two_Supreme_Kais.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20161215183033"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/05/The_two_Supreme_Kais.png/revision/latest?cb=20161215183033" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Gowasu and Shin" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/05/The_two_Supreme_Kais.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20161215183033" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="104" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="The two Supreme Kais.png" data-image-key="The_two_Supreme_Kais.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/0/05/The_two_Supreme_Kais.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20161215183033"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:The_two_Supreme_Kais.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Gowasu and Shin</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>As he and Gowasu watch the battle unfold, they see that <a href="/wiki/Fused_Zamasu" title="Fused Zamasu">Fused Zamasu</a> is unable to properly regenerate the right side of his body from the damage done by Goku's <a href="/wiki/God_Kamehameha" title="God Kamehameha">God Kamehameha</a>. While Trunks fights Fused Zamasu, Shin and Gowasu helps what remains of humanity to transfer their powers to Trunks to finish Fused Zamasu with his <a href="/wiki/Final_Hope_Slash" title="Final Hope Slash">Final Hope Slash</a>. However when he soon returns as <a href="/wiki/Infinite_Zamasu" title="Infinite Zamasu">Infinite Zamasu</a> and kills all humanity in alternate future and is about to invade the main present, Gowasu and Shin can only save Bulma, <a href="/wiki/Future_Mai" title="Future Mai">Future Mai</a>, Future Trunks, Vegeta and Goku with their strong Ki barriers. When Goku presses the Zeno Button to summon Future Zeno, Gowasu and Shin escape with the <a href="/wiki/Time_Ring" title="Time Ring">Time Ring</a> first, while Goku, Vegeta, Bulma, and the sole survivors of the alternate future multiverse, Future Mai and Future Trunks escapes with the Time Machine, and manage to get back to the main present universe.
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Universe_Survival_Saga">Universe Survival Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D13&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Universe_Survival_Saga" title="Universe Survival Saga">Universe Survival Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/a/a1/Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png/revision/latest?cb=20171008200950" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin watching the Tournament unfold" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Screenshot 2017-10-08-12-23-37.png" data-image-key="Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/a/a1/Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20171008200950"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/a/a1/Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png/revision/latest?cb=20171008200950" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin watching the Tournament unfold" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/a/a1/Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20171008200950" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="101" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Screenshot 2017-10-08-12-23-37.png" data-image-key="Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/a/a1/Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20171008200950"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Screenshot_2017-10-08-12-23-37.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin watching the Tournament unfold</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Shin, alongside Beerus, Whis, Old Kai, and Kibito, attends the Zen Exhibition Match. During the 40 hour preparation for the Tournament of Power, Shin visits other planets in order to find strong warriors for the Tournament, however he is unsuccessful. During the Tournament of Power, Shin is concerned about his fighters, wondering if they can win the Tournament. He is shown to be bothered about the fact that Krillin was knocked out because he let his guard down, however he hides it by claiming he is not bothered at all and reassures Krillin that he did his best. Later in the Tournament, when Caulifla and Kale are revealed to have received Potara from Champa to become Kefla during the tournament, Beerus forcefully snatches Shin's Potara off his ears to toss to <a href="/wiki/Android_17" title="Android 17">Android 17</a> and <a href="/wiki/Android_18" title="Android 18">Android 18</a> upon learning it is allowed. The two note the idea of a stable and powerful "<a href="/wiki/Android_35" title="Android 35">Android 35</a>", due to 17 and 18 being twins, before Whis reminds them that both 17 and 18 would be eliminated if the supposed Android 35 was defeated and knocked offstage. Beerus decides against using the Potara while Shin states that he liked the idea.
</p><p>Shin silently watches Goku's fight with <a href="/wiki/Kefla" title="Kefla">Kefla</a>. He does, however, cheer on Android 18's victory over <a href="/wiki/Ribrianne" title="Ribrianne">Brianne de Chateau</a>; however, he takes his cheers too far, causing an irritated 18 to threaten to kill him.
</p><p>Following <a href="/wiki/Universe_3" title="Universe 3">Universe 3</a>'s erasure, the <a href="/wiki/Grand_Minister" title="Grand Minister">Grand Minister</a> shrinks the viewing stands, which forces all the remaining deities and warriors physically closer together. Shin tries to politely greet <a href="/wiki/Khai" title="Khai">Khai</a> from <a href="/wiki/Universe_11" title="Universe 11">Universe 11</a>, but is ignored. He continues to watch the Tournament of Power.
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Galactic_Patrol_Prisoner_Saga">Galactic Patrol Prisoner Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D14&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Galactic_Patrol_Prisoner_Saga" title="Galactic Patrol Prisoner Saga">Galactic Patrol Prisoner Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4d/DBS_67_06.png/revision/latest?cb=20201221161157" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin plays horsey with Zeno" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="131" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="DBS 67 06.png" data-image-key="DBS_67_06.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4d/DBS_67_06.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20201221161157"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4d/DBS_67_06.png/revision/latest?cb=20201221161157" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin plays horsey with Zeno" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4d/DBS_67_06.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20201221161157" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="131" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="DBS 67 06.png" data-image-key="DBS_67_06.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/4d/DBS_67_06.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20201221161157"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:DBS_67_06.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin plays horsey with Zeno</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Shin intervenes to save Merus who had sacrificed his own existence to save Universe 7 and pleaded to the Grand Minister by offering to sacrifice his own life as punishment for his own failure in the Moro situation. Since the lives of Shin and Beerus are linked they both share a penalty by attending to Zeno and are later shown playing a game of horsey.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Dragon_Ball_GT"><i>Dragon Ball GT</i></span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D15&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Shadow_Dragon_Saga">Shadow Dragon Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D16&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Shadow_Dragon_Saga" title="Shadow Dragon Saga">Shadow Dragon Saga</a></div>
<p>Shin makes an appearance in one of <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a>'s flashbacks in "<a href="/wiki/Until_We_Meet_Again" title="Until We Meet Again">Until We Meet Again</a>".
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Super_Dragon_Ball_Heroes"><i>Super Dragon Ball Heroes</i></span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D17&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Prison_Planet_Saga">Prison Planet Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D18&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Prison_Planet_Saga" title="Prison Planet Saga">Prison Planet Saga</a></div>
<p>In the manga, Shin is on Beerus' Planet watching as Goku and Vegeta train with Whis. When Shin suggests a break, they are interrupted by <a href="/wiki/Future_Mai" title="Future Mai">Future Mai</a> who tells them that <a href="/wiki/Future_Trunks" title="Future Trunks">Future Trunks</a> has been kidnapped. Soon after <a href="/wiki/Fu" title="Fu">Fu</a> appears and says that he is Trunks' friend and that Trunks is on the <a href="/wiki/Prison_Planet" title="Prison Planet">Prison Planet</a> in another time. When Vegeta mentions rescuing him, Shin frantically tries to persuade them from travelling through time again though they go anyway. Before they leave however, he gives Future Mai a pair of Potara just encase they run into trouble.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Universal_Conflict_Saga">Universal Conflict Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D19&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Universal_Conflict_Saga" title="Universal Conflict Saga">Universal Conflict Saga</a></div>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/42/SDBH_10-1.png/revision/latest?cb=20191105222439" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin brings Goku and Vegeta to Earth" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="129" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="SDBH 10-1.png" data-image-key="SDBH_10-1.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/42/SDBH_10-1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20191105222439"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/42/SDBH_10-1.png/revision/latest?cb=20191105222439" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin brings Goku and Vegeta to Earth" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/42/SDBH_10-1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20191105222439" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="129" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="SDBH 10-1.png" data-image-key="SDBH_10-1.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/4/42/SDBH_10-1.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20191105222439"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:SDBH_10-1.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin brings Goku and Vegeta to Earth</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>In the anime, when <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a> and the others are being pinned down to the ground due to <a href="/wiki/Hearts" title="Hearts">Hearts</a>' <a href="/wiki/Gravity_Burst" title="Gravity Burst">Gravity Burst</a>, Shin appears in <a href="/wiki/Universe_11" title="Universe 11">Universe 11</a> and urges Goku to quickly use his <a href="/wiki/Instant_Transmission" title="Instant Transmission">Instant Transmission</a> to teleport everyone away.
</p><p>In the manga, Shin teleports Goku and Vegeta away from Universe 11 to the location of Hearts on <a href="/wiki/Earth" title="Earth">Earth</a> in <a href="/wiki/Universe_7" title="Universe 7">Universe 7</a> before heading off to see <a href="/wiki/Bulma" title="Bulma">Bulma</a>. When Hearts' <a href="/wiki/God_Meteor" title="God Meteor">God Meteor</a> is shattered, Shin uses his <a href="/wiki/Telekinesis" title="Telekinesis">telekinesis</a> to stop shards of it from raining down.
</p>
<div style="clear: both;"></div>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Demon_Invader_Saga">Demon Invader Saga</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D20&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Demon_Invader_Saga" title="Demon Invader Saga">Demon Invader Saga</a></div>
<p>Shin and <a href="/wiki/Kibito" title="Kibito">Kibito</a> are <a href="/wiki/Absorption" title="Absorption">absorbed</a> by <a href="/wiki/Majin_Ozotto" title="Majin Ozotto">Majin Ozotto</a> when he arrives on their <a href="/wiki/Sacred_World_of_the_Kai" title="Sacred World of the Kai">planet</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-25" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-25"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> He is later freed by Goku along with everyone else.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Other_Dragon_Ball_stories">Other <i>Dragon Ball</i> stories</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D21&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="What-if_scenarios">What-if scenarios</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D22&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<dl><dt>What-if stories</dt></dl>
<p>In the What-If Saga "<a href="/wiki/Destined_Rivals" title="Destined Rivals">Destined Rivals</a>" in <i>Budokai Tenkaichi 2</i>, Shin faces Piccolo during the 25th World Tournament, but Piccolo actually manages to defeat Shin, soon reacting with horror at what he had just done when he learns that Shin is actually the Supreme Kai. Shin is unconcerned however and decides to recruit Piccolo in trying to halt Majin Buu's resurrection at the hands of Babidi. However, he and Piccolo end up ambushed shortly upon arrival at Babidi's hideout by Babidi's right-hand man Dabura. Shin is gravely injured, while Piccolo is turned to stone by Dabura. After Goku and Vegeta effortlessly defeat Dabura and destroy Babidi's spaceship with Babidi and Majin Buu inside it, Shin expresses shock at this turn of events, with Piccolo, restored to his regular form, explaining to Goku and Vegeta what had occurred. Goku apologizes to Shin and, as thanks for stopping Buu before he could be awakened, Shin lets Vegeta and Goku resume their ultimate showdown on the Sacred World of the Kais.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Legends"><i>Legends</i></span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D23&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Legends" title="Dragon Ball Legends">Dragon Ball Legends</a></div>
<p>During the <a href="/wiki/Tournament_of_Time" title="Tournament of Time">Tournament of Time</a> in <a href="/wiki/Age_780" title="Age 780">Age 780</a>, <a href="/wiki/Beerus" title="Beerus">Beerus</a> reveals to a time-displaced teenage <a href="/wiki/Bulma" title="Bulma">Bulma</a> (from before she met Goku), <a href="/wiki/Shallot" title="Shallot">Shallot</a> (a mysterious amnesic <a href="/wiki/Saiyan" title="Saiyan">Saiyan</a>), and their mysterious ally <a href="/wiki/Zahha" title="Zahha">Zahha</a> that the <a href="/wiki/Tournament_of_Time" title="Tournament of Time">Tournament of Time</a> was set up by Beerus who was blackmailed by the true <a href="/wiki/Mastermind" class="mw-redirect" title="Mastermind">Mastermind</a> behind the tournament who had managed to successfully kidnap Shin (referred simply by his title), forcing Beerus to cooperate with his demands and have <a href="/wiki/King_Kai" title="King Kai">King Kai</a> inform the participates of the rules and the prize of a wish using the Super Dragon Balls (which were currently unusable due to the wish to revive the Universes erased during the Tournament of Power). Beerus tells them to information in an attempt to get Bulma, Shallot, and Zahha to join Team Beerus. 
</p><p>Later on, when they believe the Mastermind is <a href="/wiki/Babidi" title="Babidi">Babidi</a> due to his use of <a href="/wiki/Dark_Ki" title="Dark Ki">Dark Ki</a> to influence, empower, and control others during the tournament, Beerus sets his sights on eliminating Babidi who threatens to kill the Supreme Kai. However, it soon becomes apparent that Babidi is being manipulated as well by the Dark Ki. Thus, the true mastermind continues to keep Shin hostage. Eventually Beerus learns that Zahha is the true Mastermind's identity as he had been working as a double agent the manipulating everyone this whole time. Unfortunately, Beerus comes no closer to find Shin.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Power">Power</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D24&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<dl><dt>Manga and Anime</dt></dl>
<p>Shin has very few fighting scenes, and, as a result, his exact power is not clearly demonstrated. However, it is known that he is more powerful than his servant Kibito. <a href="/wiki/Piccolo" title="Piccolo">Piccolo</a>, at the time of the <a href="/wiki/25th_World_Martial_Arts_Tournament" class="mw-redirect" title="25th World Martial Arts Tournament">25th World Martial Arts Tournament</a>, also states that Shin is dimensions away from him. The closest clear example of his power is that he is much more powerful than <a href="/wiki/Frieza" title="Frieza">Frieza</a> (before his resurrection), due to his statement of all the Supreme Kais being able to defeat Frieza in one blow. However, he is no match against <a href="/wiki/Innocent_Buu" title="Innocent Buu">Buu</a>; during his brief fight against Buu, his attacks were able to stagger the monster, even able to blow a hole clean through Buu which would have killed most, although this barely fazed the Majin, who got right back up as if nothing happened. It is also stated that the other Supreme Kais of Universe 7 were more powerful than Shin.
</p><p>While proud of his status as a Supreme Kai, he is rather oblivious to the potential power of mortals. To which, he was amazed at the powers of <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a>, <a href="/wiki/Vegeta" title="Vegeta">Vegeta</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Gohan" title="Gohan">Gohan</a>. He is also scared of <a href="/wiki/Dabura" title="Dabura">Dabura</a> and <a href="/wiki/Yakon" title="Yakon">Yakon</a>'s respective power even prior to them becoming enslaved and enhanced by Babidi's magic. Babidi believes that he could defeat Shin in a one-on-one battle.
</p><p>In the manga version of the <a href="/wiki/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga" title='"Future" Trunks Saga'>"Future" Trunks Saga</a>, Shin engages in a fight with <a href="/wiki/Future_Zamasu" title="Future Zamasu">Future Zamasu</a> and manages to hold his own against him until Goku and Vegeta return to the future - though at that point Shin is completely at Future Zamasu's mercy.
</p><p>During the <a href="/wiki/Tournament_of_Power" title="Tournament of Power">Tournament of Power</a>, when Shin notes how <a href="/wiki/Android_18" title="Android 18">Android 18</a>'s love for <a href="/wiki/Krillin" title="Krillin">Krillin</a> was the key factor for her victory against <a href="/wiki/Ribrianne" title="Ribrianne">Ribrianne</a>, stating that it was Universe 7's Big Amour, Android 18 fires a small finger beam in anger at Shin for so openly expressing such strong and rather private emotions, leaving a wound on Shin's cheek.
</p>
<dl><dt>Statements by authors and guidebooks</dt></dl>
<p>The <i><a href="/wiki/Daizenshuu_7" class="mw-redirect" title="Daizenshuu 7">Daizenshuu 7</a></i> guidebook goes further and states that Shin possesses strength "far superior to the <a href="/wiki/Super_Namekian" title="Super Namekian">Super Namekian</a> Piccolo".<sup id="cite_ref-26" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-26"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-27" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-27"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Shin seems to possess the same level of strength as Goku from the <a href="/wiki/Cell_Games" title="Cell Games">Cell Games</a>, based on his precautions against Dabura - who is as strong as <a href="/wiki/Cell" title="Cell">Cell</a>.<sup id="cite_ref-28" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-28"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Abilities">Abilities</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D25&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<div class="tabber wds-tabber"><div class="wds-tabs__wrapper with-bottom-border"><ul class="wds-tabs"><li class="wds-tabs__tab wds-is-current" data-hash="Techniques"><div class="wds-tabs__tab-label"><a href="#">Techniques</a></div></li><li class="wds-tabs__tab" data-hash="Transformations"><div class="wds-tabs__tab-label"><a href="#">Transformations</a></div></li><li class="wds-tabs__tab" data-hash="Fusions"><div class="wds-tabs__tab-label"><a href="#">Fusions</a></div></li><li class="wds-tabs__tab" data-hash="Equipment"><div class="wds-tabs__tab-label"><a href="#">Equipment</a></div></li></ul></div><div class="wds-tab__content wds-is-current"><p class="mw-empty-elt">
</p><center><b><big>Techniques</big></b></center>
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Flight" title="Flight">Flight</a></b> – The ability to fly with the use of <i><a href="/wiki/Ki" title="Ki">ki</a></i>.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Ki_Blast" title="Ki Blast"><i>Ki</i> Blast</a></b> – The most basic form of energy wave.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Godly_ki" class="mw-redirect" title="Godly ki">Godly ki</a></b> - Being a Supreme Kai, Shin both possesses and can sense Godly ki.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Telepathy" title="Telepathy">Telepathy</a></b> – It is a way to communicate with others using one's mind. Users can also read the minds of the ones they communicate with, similar to telepathic eavesdropping.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Telekinesis" title="Telekinesis">Telekinesis</a></b> – A technique that allows the user to manipulate objects and other people with the power of one's mind.
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Supreme_Kai%27s_Hyper_Dance" title="Supreme Kai's Hyper Dance">Supreme Kai's Hyper Dance</a></b> - A team attack used by the Supreme Kais of Universe 7 in <i>Dokkan Battle</i>.</li></ul></li></ul>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/18/Shockwave.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20111015213000" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin uses a Kiai" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="144" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Shockwave.jpg" data-image-key="Shockwave.jpg" data-relevant="0" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/18/Shockwave.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20111015213000"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/18/Shockwave.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20111015213000" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin uses a Kiai" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/18/Shockwave.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20111015213000" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="144" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Shockwave.jpg" data-image-key="Shockwave.jpg" data-relevant="0" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/18/Shockwave.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20111015213000"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Shockwave.jpg" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin uses a Kiai</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/7/73/KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png/revision/latest?cb=20110212130819" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin using an Invisible Eye Blast" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png" data-image-key="KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/7/73/KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20110212130819"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/7/73/KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png/revision/latest?cb=20110212130819" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin using an Invisible Eye Blast" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/7/73/KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20110212130819" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png" data-image-key="KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/7/73/KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20110212130819"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:KaiSupremeInvisibleEyeBlast.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin using an Invisible Eye Blast</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Kiai" title="Kiai">Kiai</a></b> – The user affects the air currents around him with ki to produce powerful shockwaves in order to strike the opponent.
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Invisible_Eye_Blast" title="Invisible Eye Blast">Invisible Eye Blast</a></b> – A Kiai technique shot from the eyes.</li></ul></li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Energy%27s_Last" title="Energy's Last">Energy's Last</a></b> – Shin puts his hands forward and charges a purple energy sphere. Then, he fires the sphere in the form of an energy wave at the opponent, inflicting a high amount of damage. This ability is shown only in the anime.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Magic_Materialization" title="Magic Materialization">Magic Materialization</a></b> – A magical ability used to create physical matter out of thin air.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Supernatural_Abilities" class="mw-redirect" title="Supernatural Abilities">Supernatural Abilities</a></b> - Shin summons forth a block of <a href="/wiki/Katchin" title="Katchin">Katchin</a> and tosses it at his opponent.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Resurrection" title="Resurrection">Life Transfusion</a></b> – Shin is capable of giving his own life energy (while a living being) to a dead person, resurrecting the latter and killing the "donor". He attempts to use this power to resurrect Goku in Old Kai's place, however his ancestor declines, saying Shin is young and so Old Kai will give up his life instead.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Kai_Kai" title="Kai Kai">Kai Kai</a></b> – A technique that allows its user to instantly teleport to another planet, place or person. Unlike Instant Transmission, the user does not actually need to focus on a specific energy signature to use as a target. This means that the user can transport anywhere within and even outside the universe.</li></ul>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png/revision/latest?cb=20161123121317" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="The two Supreme Kais using an Energy Shield" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="104" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Supreme Kais Energy Shield.png" data-image-key="Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20161123121317"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png/revision/latest?cb=20161123121317" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="The two Supreme Kais using an Energy Shield" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20161123121317" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="104" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Supreme Kais Energy Shield.png" data-image-key="Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20161123121317"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Supreme_Kais_Energy_Shield.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">The two Supreme Kais using an Energy Shield</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Energy_Shield" title="Energy Shield">Energy Shield</a></b> - A technique used to generate an energy shield around the user to protect them from attacks.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Healing" title="Healing">Healing</a></b> - As a Kai, Shin possesses the ability to rejuvenate anyone and restore them to full health instantly, even if they are on the brink of death.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Life_Link" title="Life Link">Life Link</a></b> - According to Whis, Shin's and <a href="/wiki/Beerus" title="Beerus">Beerus</a>' lives are linked to one another, so if one of them dies, the other will die as well (in a manner similar to Piccolo and Kami) in order to prevent an imbalance between the natural forces of creation and destruction which Shin and Beerus represent.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Warp" title="Warp">Warp</a></b> - Used in the <a href="/wiki/Universal_Conflict_Saga" title="Universal Conflict Saga">Universal Conflict Saga</a> to save Goku, Vegeta and Future Trunks from Hearts.</li></ul>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Circular_Swing.JPG/revision/latest?cb=20131020011728" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Circular Disengagement in Super Butōden 3" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="69" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Circular Swing.JPG" data-image-key="Circular_Swing.JPG" data-relevant="0" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Circular_Swing.JPG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20131020011728"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Circular_Swing.JPG/revision/latest?cb=20131020011728" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Circular Disengagement in Super Butōden 3" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Circular_Swing.JPG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20131020011728" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="69" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Circular Swing.JPG" data-image-key="Circular_Swing.JPG" data-relevant="0" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/e/e8/Circular_Swing.JPG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20131020011728"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Circular_Swing.JPG" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Circular Disengagement in <i>Super Butōden 3</i></p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<ul><li><b>Circular Disengagement</b> – Shin swings his arms around in circles. This multiple hits attack is used in the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_But%C5%8Dden_(series)" title="Dragon Ball Z: Butōden (series)"><i>Butōden</i> series</a>, and is also known as <i>Kienjin</i>.</li>
<li><b>Crazed Assault</b> – Shin unleashes a load of crazy punches. This multiple punches attack is used in the <i>Butōden</i> series, being also called "Punch Rush" in <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Super_But%C5%8Dden_3" title="Dragon Ball Z: Super Butōden 3">Dragon Ball Z: Super Butōden 3</a></i>.</li>
<li><b>Noble Throw</b> – A multiple hits kick technique used in the <i>Butōden</i> series (named <b>Quad Kick</b> or <b>Quadruple God Kick</b>), as well as in <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Budokai_2" title="Dragon Ball Z: Budokai 2">Dragon Ball Z: Budokai 2</a></i>.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Continuous_Energy_Bullet" title="Continuous Energy Bullet">Energy Rain</a></b> – The name of the Renzoku Energy Dan technique he uses in the <i>Butōden</i> series and <i>Budokai 2</i>.</li>
<li><b>Shockwave</b> – In the <i>Butōden</i> series, Shin's Shockwave is a ground shave energy blade. He throws this <i>ki</i> blast down at the ground, and it runs along toward the opponent. It is called <i>Energy Zan</i> in <i>Super Butōden 3</i>.</li>
<li><b>Ki Thrust</b> – Shin forms a large energy sphere on his finger, and then he lets it go at the opponent. It is one of his <a href="/wiki/Super_Attack" title="Super Attack">super attacks</a> in <i>Super Butōden 3</i>.</li>
<li><b>Energy Push</b> – An energy ball fired from one hand. It is one of his super attacks in <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Ultimate_Battle_22" title="Dragon Ball Z: Ultimate Battle 22">Dragon Ball Z: Ultimate Battle 22</a></i>.</li></ul>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d9/Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png/revision/latest?cb=20120124004447" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Supreme Kai's Renzoku Energy Distortion" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="136" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Ultimate Battle 22 - Renzoku Energy Distortion.png" data-image-key="Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d9/Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20120124004447"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d9/Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png/revision/latest?cb=20120124004447" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Supreme Kai's Renzoku Energy Distortion" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d9/Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20120124004447" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="136" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Ultimate Battle 22 - Renzoku Energy Distortion.png" data-image-key="Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/d/d9/Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20120124004447"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Ultimate_Battle_22_-_Renzoku_Energy_Distortion.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Supreme Kai's Renzoku Energy Distortion</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Renzoku_Energy_Distortion" title="Renzoku Energy Distortion">Renzoku Energy Distortion</a></b> – Shin fires five energy spheres in five different directions. It is one of his super attacks in <i>Ultimate Battle 22</i>.</li>
<li><b>Holiness Break</b> – A rush attack used in <i>Budokai 2</i>.</li>
<li><b>Majestic Rush</b> – A rush attack finished with a Kiai. Used in <i>Budokai 2</i>.</li>
<li><b>Crazy Rush</b> – Shin's rush attack in the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Budokai_Tenkaichi_(series)" title="Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi (series)"><i>Budokai Tenkaichi</i> series</a>. Shin rushes at his opponent and knocks them in the air, then he proceeds to kick them around and knocks them down with a final upside down kick.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Gekiretsu_Shin%27ou%27hou" title="Gekiretsu Shin'ou'hou">Gekiretsu Shin'ou'hou</a></b> – Shin's <a href="/wiki/Ultimate_Blast" title="Ultimate Blast">ultimate attack</a> in the <i>Butōden</i> series and the <i>Budokai Tenkaichi</i> series. Shin gathers blue sparkling energy in his hands and releases a very powerful, pulsating blast.</li>
<li><b>Meteo Telekinesis</b> – Shin's <a href="/wiki/Meteor_Attack" title="Meteor Attack">Meteor Attack</a> in <i>Ultimate Battle 22</i>. He uses his telekinesis to control and attack his opponent. Also used by <a href="/wiki/Master_Roshi" title="Master Roshi">Master Roshi</a>.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Afterimage_Strike" title="Afterimage Strike">Afterimage Strike</a></b> – One of Shin's <a href="/wiki/Blast_1" title="Blast 1">Blast 1</a> in the <i>Budokai Tenkaichi</i> series.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Draw" title="Draw">Draw</a></b> - Used in <i>Dragon Ball Heroes</i>.<p class="mw-empty-elt"></p></li></ul></div><div class="wds-tab__content"><p class="mw-empty-elt">
</p><center><b><big>Transformations</big></b></center>
<dl><dt>Mini</dt></dl>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/c/c3/Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png/revision/latest?cb=20241021074909" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Mini Shin in Daima" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="348" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Daima - Mini Shin design.png" data-image-key="Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/c/c3/Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241021074909"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/c/c3/Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png/revision/latest?cb=20241021074909" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Mini Shin in Daima" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/c/c3/Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241021074909" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="348" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Daima - Mini Shin design.png" data-image-key="Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/c/c3/Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241021074909"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Daima_-_Mini_Shin_design.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Mini Shin in <i>Daima</i></p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>With the <a href="/wiki/Earth_Dragon_Ball" title="Earth Dragon Ball">Earth's Dragon Balls</a>, <a href="/wiki/Gomah" title="Gomah">Gomah</a> wishes for everyone who fought <a href="/wiki/Majin_Buu" title="Majin Buu">Majin Buu</a> to turn into children and babies in the beginning of <i>Dragon Ball Daima</i>. In this state, he is known as <b>Supreme Kai (Mini)</b>.
</p>
<div style="clear: both;"></div>
<dl><dt>Kibitoshin</dt></dl>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Kibito_Kai" title="Kibito Kai">Kibito Kai</a></div>
<figure class="thumb mw-halign-left show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/89/Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20100802132529" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin transformed into Kibitoshin" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Budokai Tenkaichi 3 - Kibito Kai.jpg" data-image-key="Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/89/Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100802132529"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/89/Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20100802132529" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin transformed into Kibitoshin" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/89/Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100802132529" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Budokai Tenkaichi 3 - Kibito Kai.jpg" data-image-key="Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/8/89/Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100802132529"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Budokai_Tenkaichi_3_-_Kibito_Kai.jpg" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin transformed into Kibitoshin</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Since Kibito is not featured in <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Budokai_Tenkaichi_2" title="Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi 2">Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi 2</a></i> and <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Budokai_Tenkaichi_3" title="Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi 3">Budokai Tenkaichi 3</a></i>, Shin transforms into <b>Kibitoshin</b> by powering up.
</p>
<div style="clear: both;"></div><p class="mw-empty-elt"></p></div><div class="wds-tab__content"><p class="mw-empty-elt">
</p><center><b><big>Fusions</big></b></center>
<dl><dt>Kibito Kai</dt></dl>
<div role="note" data-nosnippet="" class="notice hatnote context-link main dablink">Main article: <a href="/wiki/Kibito_Kai" title="Kibito Kai">Kibito Kai</a></div>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/12/KibitoKaiNV.png/revision/latest?cb=20100424162026" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Kibito Kai" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="KibitoKaiNV.png" data-image-key="KibitoKaiNV.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/12/KibitoKaiNV.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100424162026"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/12/KibitoKaiNV.png/revision/latest?cb=20100424162026" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Kibito Kai" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/12/KibitoKaiNV.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100424162026" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="135" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="KibitoKaiNV.png" data-image-key="KibitoKaiNV.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/1/12/KibitoKaiNV.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20100424162026"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:KibitoKaiNV.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Kibito Kai</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<p>Kibito Kai is the fusion taken on by Shin after using the Potara Earrings to fuse with Kibito. While their <a href="/wiki/Potara" title="Potara">Potara</a> <a href="/wiki/Fusion" title="Fusion">Fusion</a> was initially viewed as a permanent fusion like <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">Old Kai</a> (as Kibito Kai remains fused in <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_GT" title="Dragon Ball GT">Dragon Ball GT</a></i>), in <i><a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Super" title="Dragon Ball Super">Dragon Ball Super</a></i>, Kibito Kai uses the <a href="/wiki/Namekian_Dragon_Ball" title="Namekian Dragon Ball">Namekian Dragon Balls</a> to undo the fusion, causing Shin and Kibito to defuse.
</p>
<div style="clear: both;"></div><p class="mw-empty-elt"></p></div><div class="wds-tab__content"><p class="mw-empty-elt">
</p><center><b><big>Equipment</big></b></center>
<figure class="thumb  show-info-icon" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" style="width: 180px"> 	<a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/9a/Shin_clock.png/revision/latest?cb=20200604181643" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin's clock" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="182" class="thumbimage lazyload" data-image-name="Shin clock.png" data-image-key="Shin_clock.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/9a/Shin_clock.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20200604181643"></a> 	<noscript><a href="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/9a/Shin_clock.png/revision/latest?cb=20200604181643" class="mw-file-description image"><img alt="Shin's clock" src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/9a/Shin_clock.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20200604181643" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="180" height="182" class="thumbimage" data-image-name="Shin clock.png" data-image-key="Shin_clock.png" data-relevant="1" data-src="https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/dragonball/images/9/9a/Shin_clock.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20200604181643"></a></noscript> 	<figcaption class="thumbcaption"> 		 			<a href="/wiki/File:Shin_clock.png" class="info-icon"><svg><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-info-small"></use></svg></a> 		 		 		 			<p class="caption">Shin's clock</p> 		 	</figcaption> </figure>
<ul><li><b><a href="/wiki/Potara" title="Potara">Potara</a></b> - Earrings worn by Supreme Kais and their apprentices. Despite being worn so casually, they have incredible properties, allowing two individuals to fuse or permitting the wearer to use the Time Rings.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Katchin" title="Katchin">Katchin</a></b> - A material said to be one of the strongest metals in the universe.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Time_Ring" title="Time Ring">Time Ring</a></b> - Accessories of the Supreme Kais which enable them to travel through time. They are normally used to observe future events in their main timeline.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Senzu_Bean" title="Senzu Bean">Senzu Bean</a></b> - Mystical beans with immense rejuvenation properties.</li>
<li><b>Clock</b> - A clock summoned by Shin in the <a href="/wiki/%22Future%22_Trunks_Saga" title='"Future" Trunks Saga'>"Future" Trunks Saga</a> to track the amount of time a Potara Fusion has remaining.</li>
<li><b><a href="/wiki/Demon_Realm_Plane" title="Demon Realm Plane">Demon Realm Plane</a></b> - A type of vehicle that allows its users to travel between the Demon Realm and the multiverse.<p class="mw-empty-elt"></p></li></ul></div></div>
