<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="List_of_characters_killed_by_Shin">List of characters killed by Shin</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D33&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<dl><dt>Pre-<i>Dragon Ball Z</i></dt></dl>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/Bibidi" title="Bibidi">Bibidi</a> - Killed in battle by Shin.</li></ul>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Trivia">Trivia</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a title="Sign in to edit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-action="edit-section" href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fdragonball.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FShin%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D34&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" data-testid="log-in-edit-section" aria-label="Sign in to edit"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-tiny" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-tiny"></use></svg></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<ul><li>Shin's pseudonym name is derived from his title, "Kaioh<b>shin</b>", meaning "god."</li>
<li>Despite being a <a href="/wiki/Supreme_Kai_(position)" title="Supreme Kai (position)">Supreme Kai</a>, Shin is rather bad at his job due to the fact he was forced to take over after all his fellow Supreme Kais were killed or <a href="/wiki/Absorption" title="Absorption">absorbed</a> by <a href="/wiki/Kid_Buu" title="Kid Buu">Kid Buu</a>. Although, much of his mistakes were more so due to his bad decisions than inexperience.
<ul><li>Though he managed to kill <a href="/wiki/Bibidi" title="Bibidi">Bibidi</a>, he left <a href="/wiki/Innocent_Buu" title="Innocent Buu">Innocent Buu</a>'s <a href="/wiki/Sealed_Ball" title="Sealed Ball">Sealed Ball</a> on <a href="/wiki/Earth" title="Earth">Earth</a>. Unfortunately, despite knowing its location, Shin failed to keep tabs on the Earth thus was shocked by the power exhibited by the <a href="/wiki/Super_Saiyan" title="Super Saiyan">Super Saiyans</a> <a href="/wiki/Goku" title="Goku">Goku</a>, <a href="/wiki/Vegeta" title="Vegeta">Vegeta</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Gohan" title="Gohan">Gohan</a>.</li>
<li>Additionally, he elected not to inform Gohan's family and loved ones of his survival which he could have easily done so while Gohan was training by either contacting <a href="/wiki/King_Kai" title="King Kai">King Kai</a> himself or having <a href="/wiki/Kibito" title="Kibito">Kibito</a> do it. Alternatively, he could have had Kibito teleport to Earth briefly to inform the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Team" title="Dragon Team">Dragon Team</a> that Gohan was training. His failure to do either, unfortunately resulted in the death of <a href="/wiki/Chi-Chi" title="Chi-Chi">Chi-Chi</a> who was turned into an <a href="/wiki/Egg" title="Egg">Egg</a> and crushed by <a href="/wiki/Super_Buu" title="Super Buu">Super Buu</a> after she slapped the Majin because she believed his previous incarnation Innocent Buu killed her eldest son, an event witnessed by her young son <a href="/wiki/Goten" title="Goten">Goten</a> (though this had the effect of making him more dedicated to fusing into <a href="/wiki/Gotenks" title="Gotenks">Gotenks</a> to defeat Super Buu and spared her the fate of being eaten by Buu during his feeding frenzy after escaping the <a href="/wiki/Hyperbolic_Time_Chamber" title="Hyperbolic Time Chamber">Hyperbolic Time Chamber</a>).</li>
<li>He neglected to inform the Dragon Team from the beginning of the Majin Buu conflict of Majin Buu's Absorption ability and the events that lead to the Kid Buu becoming Innocent Buu. Had he done so the Dragon Team would have been better prepared. Additionally, Shin wasted time during the <a href="/wiki/25th_World_Martial_Arts_Tournament" class="mw-redirect" title="25th World Martial Arts Tournament">25th World Martial Arts Tournament</a> by acting mysterious and not approaching the Dragon Team right away.</li>
<li>Shin also never truly realized how the absorption of <a href="/wiki/Grand_Supreme_Kai" title="Grand Supreme Kai">Grand Supreme Kai</a> and Kid Buu's transformation into Innocent Buu had changed the creature, thus never thought to try to reawaken Grand Supreme Kai's memories or tried to convince Innocent Buu to stop killing like <a href="/wiki/Mr._Satan" title="Mr. Satan">Mr. Satan</a> did (though in his defense he was likely traumatized by the loss of his fellow Supreme Kai and simply saw Innocent Buu as the same monster as Kid Buu).</li>
<li>Shin lacked knowledge about items such as the <a href="/wiki/Dragon_Ball_(object)" title="Dragon Ball (object)">Dragon Balls</a> and <a href="/wiki/Potara" title="Potara">Potara</a>, which could have been valuable resources to challenge Buu at the time. Despite Buu being sealed away for millions of years, Shin did not bother to educate himself during the period of peace to learn more about the artifacts within his own universe, something <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">Old Kai</a> would admonish him for later.</li>
<li>Shin is not aware of <a href="/wiki/Zeno" title="Zeno">Zeno</a> and had to ask <a href="/wiki/Old_Kai" title="Old Kai">Old Kai</a> who he was.</li>
<li>Shin was unaware of <a href="/wiki/Future_Trunks" title="Future Trunks">Future Trunks</a>' and <a href="/wiki/Cell" title="Cell">Cell</a>'s usage of the <a href="/wiki/Time_Machine" title="Time Machine">Time Machine</a> that led to the creation of <a href="/wiki/Alternate_Timeline" title="Alternate Timeline">alternate timelines</a>, despite the formation of new green <a href="/wiki/Time_Ring" title="Time Ring">Time Rings</a> to represent that. Shin ignorantly allowed time manipulation, which is a grave sin that disrupts the cosmic balance, to occur within his Universe, which while saving Goku from the <a href="/wiki/Heart_Virus" title="Heart Virus">Heart Virus</a>, paved the possibility of <a href="/wiki/Zamasu" title="Zamasu">Zamasu</a> becoming <a href="/wiki/Goku_Black" title="Goku Black">Goku Black</a>.</li>
<li>Due to <a href="/wiki/Universe_7" title="Universe 7">Universe 7</a> having the second lowest <a href="/wiki/Mortal_Level" title="Mortal Level">Mortal Level</a>, <a href="/wiki/Beerus" title="Beerus">Beerus</a> blames Shin for choosing to let the mortals develop on their own instead of providing guidance while Shin blame Beerus for not doing his job too.</li></ul></li></ul>
